PR solve?\r\n\r\n- Closes #120214\r\n\r\n- #119871 caused two regressions in addition to #119979.\r\n\r\n1. The key acquisition range in cases where playback is slowed down by `stretch_time_scale` has become broken\r\n2. `start_offset` no longer functions in `stretch_time_scale`; This prevents the adjustment of the start position for the period of time-adjusted walking cycles\r\n\r\n- I will partially revert #119871 with keeping some lines for the start-end section to prevent the recurrence of the issue with #118101\r\n\r\n**Revert:**\r\n\r\n- The change to `cur_len` definition and change usage of `anim_size` causes issue 1, so this must be reverted\r\n- Removing `start_offset` from the time calculation causes issue 2, so this must be reverted\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n- I tested #119988 locally, and all tests passed except for the cases where `start_offset` is valid with stretched `custom_timeline`. The test cases for `stretch_time_scale` with `start_offset` in #119988 are based on the results from a regression in #119871, so the expected values of the tests are incorrect in the first place\r\n\r\nSimply put, what was needed for #119871 compared to #119846 was at most the handling for Backward at https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/119871#discussion_r3336380354, as we discussed in https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/119846#pullrequestreview-4381786505.\r\n\r\ncc @chocola-mint \r\n","labels":[{"id":73330064,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2NA==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/bug","name":"bug","description":"","color":"ff6055","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":1332303119,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwxMzMyMzAzMTE5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/regression","name":"regression","description":"","color":"ff63ac","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":2666705648,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNjY2NzA1NjQ4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:anim